## Goal (from TODO.md, item now removed in this branch)
Before this work, only documents and mail kept their bytes as `CONTENT` rows under `content/`. Every other Blob cell named an object in a folder of its own: photos, pronunciations, flyers, report screenshots, image-search stock, wiki pictures and per-app upload folders.

The task is to make every stored byte a reference to a `CONTENT` row:
- Blob columns become `CONTENT` refs.
- Uploads become `CONTENT` rows; the app image folders, `imageFolders`, the per-app folder routes and the `-thumb.jpg` objects go away.
- `CONTENT`'s read policy gains a clause for each referencing column, keeping originals private.
- The sweeper deletes whatever nothing references.
- Flyers and wiki pictures get `PHOTO`'s treatment: a private original plus a served re-encode with every tag dropped (issue #159).
- Existing objects move with a one-off `local/` tool.

