![](/api/wiki/picture/f6003662be5e165688ecb85e70d19e6e1088bdc9f6c4086aa8dd8ce04bfafb09.jpg)
```
and `GET /api/wiki/picture/{name}` serves `wiki-images/f600…fb09.jpg` exactly as uploaded, tags and all, to anyone signed in.

**The goal.** The original and the re-encode are both `CONTENT` rows held by a row. Only the tag-free re-encode is served. `wiki-images/` and `/api/wiki/picture/` go away.

**The same picture on "Room Parent Guide", each way:**

- (*) A PHOTO of the page
  `PHOTO` gains a `document` column, so a photo is of a person, a group or a wiki page, exactly one. The picture becomes `PHOTO pho… {document: docwsi7bPlEKXO, original: con…(the jpg as uploaded)}`. The existing photo worker makes its `reencode` and `thumbnail`, and the markdown becomes `![](/api/blob/pho…/image)`. That address serves the re-encode, and the original stays private as every photo's does. It's read by whoever reads the page.
  Inserting a picture posts it to `/api/do/photo` with the page. On a page that has never been saved, the editor saves it first. Saving the page deletes the page's photos its markdown no longer names.
